 "text": "Hi, how are you holding up? Stay calm and breathe. First, ask if the venue has a back entrance for you to use. No, walking in just before the couple appear on stage. Text them first so they' expecting you. Then head straight to your seat and try to blend in. Find a reputable taxi or book ahead a car. Being stuck in a crowd is riskier. The wedding will still be happening without you. That's the thing about being late, it gives you perspective. Focus on enjoying the ceremony and chatting to your partner about what you'd have been doing if you weren't late.",
